  the three upper-limit discs, per disc (nu_mono, canonical, alpha = 3.36): delta_route is a LOWER bound on that disc's delta under the law shown
    CRISTAL-08   z 4.430  f_molgas <= 0.63:  delta_flat >= +0.553, delta_rival >= +0.264   (fit route: +0.387, +0.130)
    CRISTAL-12   z 5.572  f_molgas <= 0.67:  delta_flat >= +0.219, delta_rival >= -0.093   (fit route: +0.281, -0.044)
    CRISTAL-23b  z 4.562  f_molgas <= 0.25:  delta_flat >= -0.261, delta_rival >= -0.360   (fit route: +0.443, +0.188)
    -> discs whose lower bound is above 0: flat 2 of 3, rival 1 of 3 (a lower bound above 0 means the law UNDER-predicts that disc's mass discrepancy whatever the true, smaller, gas mass)

  the lane's 'SED + gas: both laws CONSISTENT for the 9 disks that have both' rests on six detections and three upper limits used as values; the six-detection cells and the one-sided bounds are above
